    "b-15-worktrees-a-run-against-a-reposito-1": {
      "id": "b-15-worktrees-a-run-against-a-reposito-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A run against a repository works in its own git worktree by default: a separate checkout of the same repository on its own branch. Two runs can edit "
        },
        {
          "insert": "auth.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " at the same time without seeing each other's changes, and a run's ordinary edits stay in its worktree instead of your checkout. If you don't like the result, close the pull request."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-15-worktrees-a-worktree-separates-che-2": {
      "id": "b-15-worktrees-a-worktree-separates-che-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A worktree separates checkouts. It is not an execution or security sandbox: commands a run executes can still affect files outside it. For an isolated execution environment on a folder project, see "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Container isolation",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "docs/30-authoring/20-guides/70-container-isolation.md",
              "label": "Container isolation"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-15-worktrees-choose-how-a-run-is-isol-3": {
      "id": "b-15-worktrees-choose-how-a-run-is-isol-3",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Choose how a run is isolated"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "table-0-38be0e38": {
      "id": "table-0-38be0e38",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Command",
          "Behavior"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            [
              {
                "insert": "archon workflow run <name> \"...\"",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            "New worktree on a generated branch"
          ],
          [
            [
              {
                "insert": "archon workflow run <name> --branch fix/login \"...\"",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            "Reuses a healthy Archon registration for the branch, otherwise creates or reuses a worktree at the configured target path"
          ],
          [
            [
              {
                "insert": "archon workflow run <name> --no-worktree \"...\"",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            "Runs in your current checkout"
          ]
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-15-worktrees-use-branch-with-a-de-5": {
      "id": "b-15-worktrees-use-branch-with-a-de-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Use "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--branch",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " with a descriptive name for work that changes code; it makes worktrees and pull requests easy to identify. Use "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--no-worktree",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " only for read-only work. A workflow can pin the choice with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worktree.enabled",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " in its YAML. Don't start two runs on the same branch at once: one branch maps to one worktree."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-15-worktrees-by-default-worktrees-li-6": {
      "id": "b-15-worktrees-by-default-worktrees-li-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "By default, worktrees live under "
        },
        {
          "insert": "~/.archon/workspaces/<owner>/<repo>/worktrees/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Set "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worktree.path",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " in the repository's config for a repo-local location such as "
        },
        {
          "insert": ".worktrees",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and add it to "
        },
        {
          "insert": ".gitignore",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-15-worktrees-with-branch-archon-7": {
      "id": "b-15-worktrees-with-branch-archon-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "With "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--branch",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", Archon first reuses a healthy active task worktree registered in Archon for that project and branch, even at another path. Without that registration, worktree creation can still reuse a usable checkout at the configured target path. Both reuse paths verify the checkout is on the requested branch. A different branch or detached HEAD causes a refusal that names the requested branch, actual branch, and checkout path; Archon leaves the checkout unchanged. If no healthy active task registration was reused and another path holds the branch, creation fails with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "branch_checked_out",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", naming the holder, whether or not it is registered in Archon. Check whether a live Archon run still needs that checkout before freeing the branch. Once it is safe, preserve its changes, then detach it with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "git -C <holder-path> switch --detach",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " or remove it before retrying. Archon leaves that checkout untouched. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Exact-branch continuation",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "docs/10-system-design/10-reference/20-cli.md",
              "section": "continuing-an-existing-estate",
              "label": "Exact-branch continuation"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", such as "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--adopt",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", can reuse a Git-registered holder at another path."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-15-worktrees-a-workflow-can-also-star-8": {
      "id": "b-15-worktrees-a-workflow-can-also-star-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A workflow can also start a child run with its own worktree by writing "
        },
        {
          "insert": "isolation: worktree",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " on a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "workflow:",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " node; see "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Launching a separate governed run",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "docs/10-system-design/10-reference/35-workflow-language.md",
              "section": "launching-a-separate-governed-run-with-workflow",
              "label": "Launching a separate governed run"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Those branches have generated names such as "
        },
        {
          "insert": "archon/task-3f9a1c2b-...-child-0",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". A paused or failed child run resumes in its original worktree, so leave child worktrees alone until the whole run has finished."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-15-worktrees-provision-new-worktrees-9": {
      "id": "b-15-worktrees-provision-new-worktrees-9",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Provision new worktrees"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-15-worktrees-prepare-dependencies-and-10": {
      "id": "b-15-worktrees-prepare-dependencies-and-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Prepare dependencies and generated files before agents start, in the repository's "
        },
        {
          "insert": ".archon/config.yaml",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ":"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-15-worktrees-yaml-11": {
      "id": "b-15-worktrees-yaml-11",
      "type": "code",
      "props": {
        "language": "yaml"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "worktree:\n  copyFiles: ['.env']\n  postCreate:\n    - bun install --frozen-lockfile\n  postCreateTimeout: 300000     # per command, in milliseconds"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-15-worktrees-commands-run-in-order-in-12": {
      "id": "b-15-worktrees-commands-run-in-order-in-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Commands run in order in the new checkout, after submodules and copied files. A command that exits nonzero, times out or cannot start stops worktree creation, and the error reports the exit code or timeout with the command's output. Both a healthy Archon-registered worktree and a usable existing checkout at the configured target path are reused without running setup again. Setup should provision the checkout, not leave a server running. Copied "
        },
        {
          "insert": ".env",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " files are not loaded automatically. See "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Configuration",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "docs/10-system-design/10-reference/55-configuration.md",
              "label": "Configuration"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " for every "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worktree",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " option."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-15-worktrees-inspect-and-clean-up-13": {
      "id": "b-15-worktrees-inspect-and-clean-up-13",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Inspect and clean up"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-15-worktrees-bash-14": {
      "id": "b-15-worktrees-bash-14",
      "type": "code",
      "props": {
        "language": "bash"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "archon isolation list                         # active worktrees and containers\narchon isolation cleanup                      # remove eligible environments older than 7 days\narchon isolation cleanup 14                   # ... older than 14 days\narchon isolation cleanup --merged             # remove environments whose branches merged\narchon isolation cleanup --merged --include-closed   # also those whose PRs closed unmerged\narchon complete fix/login                     # remove a branch's worktree and local branch; retain its remote branch"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-15-worktrees-cleanup-keeps-live-runs-15": {
      "id": "b-15-worktrees-cleanup-keeps-live-runs-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Cleanup keeps live runs, resumable failed runs, worktrees with uncommitted changes and commits that exist on no remote. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--merged",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "archon complete",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " retain remote branches with a warning, including with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--force",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", because registration ownership cannot be proved after local cleanup. Enable GitHub's "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Automatically delete head branches",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " setting for merged pull requests, or follow "
        },
        {
          "insert": "manual remote branch recovery",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "docs/10-system-design/10-reference/20-cli.md",
              "section": "recovering-remote-branch-cleanup",
              "label": "manual remote branch recovery"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". A run launched without "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--branch",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " removes the worktree it created on its own generated branch when it completes, if the worktree is clean and Archon confirms every commit is on a remote, keeping the local and remote branch. Otherwise the worktree stays, the run's output names the path and what removing it would lose, and its terminal record keeps the reason. A workflow launched from the Web UI gets the same per-run worktree and the same removal. A worktree created for "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--branch",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " stays when the run ends; "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--merged",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " or "
        },
        {
          "insert": "archon complete",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " removes it. A worktree that belongs to a chat conversation, an issue or a pull request rather than to one run also stays; "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--merged",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", or "
        },
        {
          "insert": "archon isolation cleanup",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " once it is stale, removes it. A workflow with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worktree.enabled: false",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " creates no worktree."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-15-worktrees-without-a-server-schedu-16": {
      "id": "b-15-worktrees-without-a-server-schedu-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Without a server, schedule merged cleanup with the SDLC pack's "
        },
        {
          "insert": "archon-worktree-cleanup",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " workflow. A failed run keeps its worktree so you can resume it with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "archon workflow resume <run-id>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", or discard it with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "archon workflow abandon <run-id>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", which attempts worktree removal while keeping the branch. Owner warnings retain the checkout for inspection: use "
        },
        {
          "insert": "lsof",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " when output is still held, resolve the warning, then retry abandonment on the cancelled run."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  }
}
